paper/main.tex:161:\textbf{Keyword pruning backfired on the matched cases.} Full-context accuracy was \pruningFullAccuracy{}\%, compared with \pruningPrunedAccuracy{}\% after filtering, a change of \pruningChange{} points [\pruningChangeLow{}, \pruningChangeHigh{}] across \pruningFamilyCount{} families. Only \pruningWins{} case improved; \pruningLosses{} worsened and \pruningTies{} tied (Table~\ref{tab:pruning}). The mechanism follows from the probe design: the filter retains the competing clause because it repeats the question's words, while the paraphrased answer clause has less lexical overlap.
paper/main.tex:193:The controls support this explanation without proving it for other tasks. Literal wording improved matched accuracy by \literalControlChange{} points, with \literalControlWins{} wins and no losses. Across all outputs, distractor capture was \distractorCaptureRate{}\%, exact-output compliance was \exactOutputComplianceRate{}\%, and invalid output was \invalidOutputRate{}\%. The failures therefore arose mainly from selecting the competing code, not from ignoring the requested format.
